<title>GERMANY: German 97 grain crop put at 42-43.5 mln T - co-ops.</title>
<headline>German 97 grain crop put at 42-43.5 mln T - co-ops.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's 1997 grain crop is estimated in a range between 42.0 and 43.5 million tonnes after 42.1 million in 1996, the umbrella organisation of farm co-operatives, DRV, said in a report on Friday.</p>
<p>Latest yield indications pointed to a crop size near 43 million, but forecasts could not be more precise a few weeks ahead of the completion of the harvest, a DRV grains analyst said.</p>
<p>The Bonn farm ministry a week ago said the crop should be slightly above last year's result while grain trader Toepfer maintains a forecast for 43 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The grain area for the 1997 harvest was expanded by 4.7 percent to 7.02 million hectares.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
